.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NQDRPT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdrpt
.Nd a report of a capsule and its data record
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Fd #define NQDMD 1
.Fd #define NQDTXT 2
.Ft int
.Fo nqdrpt
.Fa "const char *dir" "const nqrep *crep" "const nqdrep *drep" "int fmt"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqdrpt
writes a report of the capsule in
.Fa dir
to
.Fa out
.Pf ( Fa cap
bytes, a NUL added), in Markdown
.Pq Dv NQDMD
or plain text
.Pq Dv NQDTXT :
a line saying whether every check passed and how many of how many
failed; the rows of
.Fa crep ,
the capsule's check
.Pq Xr nqchk 3 ,
or, when
.Fa crep
is
.Dv NULL
(a folder not sealed), a line saying so, which counts as a failed
check; then a section on the data record
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5 :
its sources, schemas, drift summaries (and whether they are
calibrated), environment, steps, recorded checks, commitments and
citation, and the rows of
.Fa drep
.Pq Xr nqdchk 3 ,
each named
.Ql data. Ns Ar check ;
with
.Fa drep
.Dv NULL ,
.Fn nqdchk
is run here.
A folder without a record has no data rows.
.Pp
A value of the record never breaks its line or its table cell: a line
break or other control character in it is a space, and in Markdown
each character Markdown could read as markup
.Pq Ql "\e \(ga * _ [ ] < > | # ~ & !"
gets one backslash before it, once.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ;
.Dv NQEBUF
with
.Fa *outlen
set to the report's length when
.Fa cap
is too small;
.Dv NQEARG
for a
.Fa dir
of
.Dv NULL
or another
.Fa fmt ;
.Dv NQEMEM .
A record that does not read is a failed
.Ql data.record
row, not an error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-report 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqdchk 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
